    fix(admissions): drop the entry fields nothing resolves, close the prefix
    
    Wave-17 monitor review of b72-bootstrap raised three defects in the entry
    shape. All three are the same class -- a check whose text claims more than
    its mechanism does.
    
    `authorized_head` and `refs` were validated with their own diagnostics and
    never read by anything: a grep of the branch finds each field only inside
    its own validation. A documented pin no process resolves is the exact
    failure this repository admits skills to detect, so both are deleted rather
    than demoted to comments. The digest and the argv are what `bootstrap_checks`
    resolves; the landing commit is where the reviewed head and the issue live,
    and `git log` is what reads them back.
    
    `skills/<skill>/../../scripts/anything.py` satisfied the prefix test that was
    supposed to bind an entry to its own Skill's tree. A prefix is only a binding
    when a path cannot lie about where it points, so no argv part may be absolute
    or carry a spelling `normpath` would change. Drilled both ways against the
    pre-fix module: `03f4764` returns no errors for that argv, this commit returns
    `BOOTSTRAP_ENTRY_ARGV_UNNORMALIZED:dynamic-workflow:...`.
    
    The control that reads the live allowlist asserted the whole of
    `check_admissions.check(ROOT)`, so any unrelated admission defect anywhere in
    the repository would have reddened a control that owns one mechanism.
    `run_all.py` runs `check_admissions.py` whole already; these controls now read
    only their own `BOOTSTRAP_` diagnostics, in the live tree and in every planted
    copy.
    
    Refs ed3c/skill-concerns#72

